# 0010. Alt-h/j/k/l moves across nvim splits and tmux panes (smart-splits)

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

The same Alt keys move between and resize nvim splits and tmux panes, as if they were one
thing.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: nvim runs inside tmux; moving between nvim splits and tmux panes needed
  different keys.
- **nvim side** (`lua/plugins/tmux.lua`): `mrjones2014/smart-splits.nvim`, `lazy = false` so
  it marks the tmux pane as nvim (`@pane-is-vim`) from the start. Keys: `<A-h/j/k/l>` move
  (`move_cursor_*`), `<A-H/J/K/L>` resize by 3 (`resize_*`). Options:
  `move = { at_edge = "stop" }` (no wrap to the other side, as in tmux),
  `resize = { amount = 3 }`. Outside tmux the same keys work on nvim splits only.
- **tmux side** (`~/projects/tmux/conf/keys.conf`): `bind -n M-h if -F '#{@pane-is-vim}'
  { send-keys M-h } { if -F '#{pane_at_left}' {} { select-pane -L } }`, and the same for
  j/k/l: in an nvim pane the key goes to nvim, otherwise tmux moves, and stops at the window
  edge. At the edge of nvim's splits, smart-splits moves on to the tmux pane.
- **Kept keys**: `<C-h>`/`<C-l>` stay side-scroll (in insert mode, snippet jumps), so they
  were not used for navigation.
- **Consequences**: one set of keys, one mental model. The binding is split across two repos
  (nvim and tmux) that must agree. Upstream option renames are silent: `at_edge` was
  ignored for weeks until fixed in PR #2; check `:checkhealth smart-splits` after updates.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: smart-splits.nvim, tmux user options.
- Alternatives: `<C-h/j/k/l>` (vim-tmux-navigator style): already taken by side-scroll and
  snippet jumps here.
